From 8fb39bf87ce44224bd27925e3c0889ca7c478d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Feed the chat from the database instead of the request
 body
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chat page loads GET /api/analysis/latest on open and posts whatever it
gets back as health_data. That endpoint never existed — app/api/analysis.py
defines /trends, /metrics/latest, /metrics/history and /summary — so the load
failed every time, health_data arrived as null, and _prepare_health_context
rendered "Žiadne zdravotné dáta nie sú momentálne dostupné." The model then
answered exactly that, while the database held 265 health records and 50,860
Apple Health rows.

Two changes, either of which fixes the symptom; together they also stop it
coming back:

- app/analysis/chat_context.py builds the context server-side from the same
  loaders the rest of the API uses, so an answer no longer depends on what the
  client remembered to send. It carries the data inventory per source, the
  latest value and status per metric, daily aggregates for the recent window,
  trends, family history and the ML risk scores. Apple Health is aggregated per
  metric per day, never listed, and the whole block is capped, so the prompt
  stays bounded no matter how much history accumulates.

- GET /api/analysis/latest now exists, in the shape the deployed frontend
  expects, so that page stops falling into its error branch and its greeting
  reflects the data that is actually there.

The system prompt gains today's date and an instruction for the case the user
hit: when the asked-for window has no measurements, report the latest available
values with their dates rather than claiming there is no data at all.

