From 2d90857ec44ba169419f9995b46db0ba2a49d606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Let the chat fetch history the prompt does not carry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The context is a fixed snapshot: latest value per metric, trends, a recent
window of daily aggregates, family history, documents and the passages matching
the question. That is the right trade for most questions and it costs the same
tokens every time — which is also why it cannot carry years of per-day history
for every metric. Asked "ako mi šiel LDL za posledné dva roky" the model had
only the latest value and a trend label to answer from.

- app/chat_tools.py exposes two tools: get_metric_history for a series over an
  arbitrary range, and search_documents for report text beyond the passages
  already in the prompt. Family history, risk scores and the document list stay
  in the context, so no tool for them — that would only add a round trip.
- chat_context.metric_history adapts its granularity: daily while the range can
  be listed day by day, monthly once it cannot, so a two-year question gets a
  complete monthly series rather than a series silently cut off at the cap.
- The loop in _ask_claude runs at most MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS times and then takes one
  final turn with the tools withheld, because a tool_use turn carries no text
  and returning it would show the patient an empty reply. A failing tool comes
  back as an error string, not an exception: "toto sa mi nepodarilo zistiť" is
  a better answer than a 500 for the whole question.
- The Anthropic call now runs in a thread. It was already blocking; with
  several round trips per question it would hold the event loop far longer.

Only the Claude path gets tools. The Mistral branch is left as it was — it is
currently dead anyway, since the Railway variable is named "MISTRAL_API_KEY "
with a trailing space and never reaches settings.

tests/ covers the parts that can run without fastapi, anthropic or sqlalchemy,
which are not installed in the sandbox this was written in: the aggregation
against real pandas frames shaped like TrendAnalyzer's, BM25 ranking including
Slovak inflection and diacritics, the rendered prompt, and the tool loop driven
by a scripted client. Run them with `python tests/test_tools.py`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SUjLLy2enx9LeWY7if66cK
