Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Stop tracking .env, document the variables instead

.gitignore has listed .env since the beginning, but the file was committed
anyway and this repository is public, so WITHINGS_CLIENT_SECRET has been
readable by anyone who found it. Untracking stops it going further; it does
NOT remove it from history, so the secret still has to be rotated at
developer.withings.com and the history rewritten or the repo made private.

.env.example documents the variables without values, including the trailing
space in the Railway variable name that keeps MISTRAL_API_KEY from loading.

