From f143b6e22fc89bf25c1540e5df3d7d4830d4f98b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Rewrite the new tests in the style of the existing suite
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The three files added with the tool work were written as standalone scripts
that stubbed pandas, app.database and the analyzers by assigning into
sys.modules. That runs fine on its own and is wrong here: this repo already has
a pytest suite, and pytest imports every test module into one process, so those
global stubs would have been in place for test_sources, test_units and the
Apple Health tests too — breaking a green suite as a side effect of adding
coverage.

Now they are plain pytest: fixtures and monkeypatch, nothing assigned into
sys.modules, real pandas frames shaped the way TrendAnalyzer builds them, and
one behaviour per test with a name that says what breaks.

Also adds the forms of byť/mať and the filler words a spoken question carries
to the retrieval stopwords. "ak by som" tokenized to ["som"] and matched every
chunk containing it, which is noise ranked as signal.

53 tests: the context assembly including the empty-window branch that produced
the original bug report, BM25 ranking through Slovak inflection and diacritics,
the history aggregation, and the tool loop driven by a scripted client.

